<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles George Gordon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1833–1885</span> · Also known as Gordon of Khartoum, Chinese Gordon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles George Gordon was a British army officer who commanded the Ever Victorious Army against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiping-rebellion">Taiping</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. As governor-general of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a> for the Khedivate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> from 1877 to 1879 he campaigned against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">slave trade</a>. Sent back in 1884 to evacuate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khartoum">Khartoum</a>, he was besieged by the Mahdist forces and killed when the city fell in January 1885.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-george-gordon.jpg" alt="Charles George Gordon" width="279" height="417" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Geruzet Frères - Belgian (active c. 1870-1889) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Charles_George_Gordon_by_Freres.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
